    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0621" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg579"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 28, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 23d instant, asking to be made acquainted with the
                    cause of the arrest and <pb facs="0622" n="580" xml:id="pg580"/> imprisonment of
                    a Mr. J. Hardcastle, who is now confined in the Old Capitol prison, and to state
                    that it has been referred to Major L. C. Turner, judge advocate, with a view of
                    being enabled to satisfy the inquiry.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
